        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): replace blocking sync I/O with async in auth/credential paths (fixes #78805)",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nReplaces blocking synchronous filesystem/Keychain I/O with async equivalents in auth/credential paths. Sync `execSync` calls for macOS Keychain access blocked the Node.js event loop for 4+ seconds, causing WebSocket timeouts, infinite pending states, and duplicate message sends under concurrent agent starts.\n\n## Linked context\n\nCloses #78805\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Test Results (vitest 4.1.9)\n\nRebased onto origin/main (b3301e32127).\n\n```\n✓ src/agents/sessions/auth-storage.test.ts (3 tests, 100% pass, 2.37s)\n```\n\n### Commands\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs --config test/vitest/vitest.agents-core.config.ts src/agents/sessions/auth-storage.test.ts\n```\n\n### Before/After\n\n- Before: `execSync(\"security find-generic-password\")` blocked event loop for 4+ seconds\n- After: `execAsync` returns immediately without blocking\n\n### What was not tested\n\nLive macOS Keychain access (unit tests mock exec; requires macOS device)\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- Did user-visible behavior change? No\n- Did config, environment, or migration behavior change? No\n- Did security, auth, secrets, network, or tool execution behavior change? Yes - credential reads now async\n- What is the highest-risk area? Keychain access timeout and error handling\n- How is that risk mitigated? Same timeout values, same error paths, just promisified\n\nRebased onto origin/main (b3301e32127). Merge conflict resolved in auth-storage.ts. Latest commit: 75b3a51534d",
